{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And now, Israel</b> etc. It refers to the beginning of the book (of Numbers). Remember and reflect: that after HaShem did for you all these benefits, from the giving of the Torah until now, you angered before Him several times, and because of you I was driven from entering the land. From here onward, hear the statutes and accept instruction from them, and all is forgiven." "<b>That you may live.</b> For the worshippers of Peor were destroyed." "<b>And you shall come and inherit.</b> Lest you say: it has already been said, 'To these the land shall be divided' — to us the land is given whether righteous or wicked — do not say so, for your entry into the land depends only on the merit that you heed <b>the statutes and the judgments</b>, as he proceeds to explain."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:51:33.603694038Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}